cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Riak in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Riak: Self-contained Causal Prediction Engine"
authors:
  - github: irwanformal-cmd
abstract: >-
  Riak turns a piece of text (a news story, a policy draft, a decision, a
  "what if" question) into a branching cause-effect web of events, then
  computes the most likely outcome chain through it. It runs with zero
  dependencies (Python standard library only) using a deterministic
  rule-based causal engine, with optional upgrades via any
  OpenAI-compatible LLM.
repository-code: "https://github.com/irwanformal-cmd/riak"
url: "https://github.com/irwanformal-cmd/riak"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - causal-inference
  - prediction-engine
  - monte-carlo
  - decision-support
  - offline-first
  - zero-dependencies
  - python
version: 1.0.0
